# Architecture & Folder Structure

## Top-level layout

```
src/
├── app/                    # Next.js routes only — thin pages that compose features
├── features/               # Domain modules (auth, organizations, invoices, …)
├── components/             # Shared, domain-agnostic UI (ui/, layout/, feedback/)
├── lib/                    # Cross-cutting utilities (api/, utils/, constants/)
├── stores/                 # Zustand stores (UI state only)
├── types/                  # Shared global types
├── assets/                 # Bundled static files (imported in code)
└── mocks/                  # MSW handlers and mock data
```

## Static assets

Two locations — choose based on how the file is used:

| Location | Served at | Use when |
|----------|-----------|----------|
| `public/images/…` | `/images/…` | Logos, OG images, favicon, downloadable files, stable URLs |
| `src/assets/…` | Bundled import | Component-only images, build-time optimization |
| `src/features/{feature}/assets/` | Bundled import | Asset used by a single feature only |

Register public paths in `src/lib/constants/assets.ts`. See `public/images/README.md` and `src/assets/README.md`.

## Feature module structure

Each feature under `src/features/{feature-name}/` follows the same shape:

```
features/organizations/
├── components/             # Feature-specific components
├── hooks/                  # useOrganizations, useOrgMembers, …
├── schemas.ts              # Zod schemas
├── types.ts                # Feature types (until OpenAPI codegen replaces them)
├── api.ts                  # Ky calls or query/mutation functions
├── constants.ts            # Feature constants (optional)
└── index.ts                # Public barrel export — only expose what other features need
```

### Rules

- **`app/` pages are thin** — import from `@/features/...`, no business logic in `page.tsx`.
- **No cross-feature deep imports** — import via `@/features/foo` barrel, not `@/features/foo/components/internal/...`.
- **Colocate by feature** — if only one feature uses it, keep it inside that feature.
- **Promote to `components/`** when used by 2+ features.

## `app/` routing conventions

```
app/
├── (auth)/                 # Route group — no auth required
│   └── login/page.tsx
├── (dashboard)/            # Route group — authenticated layout
│   ├── layout.tsx
│   ├── dashboard/page.tsx
│   └── organizations/
│       ├── page.tsx
│       └── [id]/page.tsx
└── layout.tsx              # Root layout (RTL, providers, fonts)
```

- Use **route groups** `(auth)` / `(dashboard)` for layout boundaries.
- Dynamic segments: `[id]`, `[...slug]` — folder names match Next.js conventions.
- `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx` colocated per route segment when needed.

## `lib/` conventions

```
lib/
├── api/
│   ├── client.ts           # Ky instance (auth, retry, error parsing)
│   ├── query-client.ts     # TanStack Query client config
│   └── generated/          # OpenAPI codegen output (do not edit manually)
└── utils/
    ├── format-money.ts
    └── format-date.ts
```

## `components/` conventions

```
components/
├── ui/                     # Thin wrappers around antd if needed
├── layout/                 # AppShell, Sidebar, Header, PageHeader
└── feedback/               # EmptyState, ErrorAlert, LoadingSpinner
```

## File naming

| Content | File name |
|---------|-----------|
| Page | `page.tsx` (in `app/` only) |
| Layout | `layout.tsx` |
| Component | `{component-name}.tsx` |
| Hook | `use-{name}.ts` |
| Store | `{name}-store.ts` |
| Test | `{name}.test.ts` or `{name}.spec.ts` |
| MSW handler | `{feature}.handlers.ts` |

One default export component per file. Name the file after the component.
